.Dd October 2023
.Dt RETRO-RUNTIME 1
.Os
.Sh RETRO-RUNTIME
.Nm retro-runtime
.Nd "host runtime for working with a Retro image"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl t Ar filename
.Op Fl f Ar filename
.Op Fl p Ar filename
.Op Fl u Ar image
.Op Fl r Ar image
.Op Ar filename
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the non-embedded version of the Retro runtime. Unlike
.Xr retro 1 ,
it does not contain an integral image. Supply an image with
.Fl u
or
.Fl r
before loading source files or entering interactive mode.
.Pp
It is primarily a build-time tool. The Retro build uses it with
.Fl u
to load package source into the temporary
.Pa rre.image
image. It is not installed as part of the normal Retro distribution.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Fl h
Display a help screen.
.It Fl i
Start Retro in interactive mode.
.It Fl v
Run in verbose mode, showing debugging information. Verbose output is written to /dev/stderr.
.It Fl t Ar filename
Run any code and test blocks in the specified file.
.It Fl f Ar filename
Run any code blocks in the specified file.
.It Fl p Ar filename
Run the code in the specified file.
.It Fl u Ar image
Load and use the specified image file.
.It Fl r Ar image
Load and use the specified image file, then start Retro in interactive mode.
.It Ar filename
Run code blocks in a single file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Load an image and run the code blocks in a source file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
retro-runtime -u rre.image -f package/list.forth
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr retro 1
